  if hc == np.search(node1, node2):
    return hc
  return np.search(node1, node2)```This function takes two arguments: the nodes to be searched and the hc to be found. It then uses a search algorithm to find the hc of the two nodes in the binary tree. The search algorithm uses a combination of a heuristic and a brute-force search to find the hc of the two nodes. The hc is then returned as a list of heuristics that can be used to find the hc of the two nodes.
