The stages of life shape our understanding of time and mortality in many ways. As we grow and develop, we learn more about the world around us and our place in it. This can lead to a greater appreciation for the finite nature of life and the importance of cherishing the moments we have.

As we age, we may also experience changes in our physical and mental health, which can make us more aware of our own mortality. This can lead to a greater sense of urgency and a desire to make the most of our time on Earth.

Additionally, the stages of life can provide a sense of perspective on our own mortality. For example, as we approach our twenties, we may begin to think more about our long-term goals and the impact we want to have on the world. This can help us to make more informed decisions about our lives and the choices we make.

